  "prefLabel": "Ch 501.02 Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ch 501.02 Definitions. \"Sexual misconduct\" means engaging in one or more of the following activities with respect to a current client who is not a spouse or civil union partner:\n\n(a) Engaging in sexual relations, whether consensual or non-consensual;\n\n(b) Making verbal or physical sexual advances;\n\n(c) Using sexual language or phrases;\n\n(d) Requesting sexual favors; or\n\n(e) Engaging in physical contact of a sexual nature.\n\nSource. #14143, eff 12-6-24, EXPIRES: 12-6-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ch100-500.html"
}
